Date Class is the class that we use in day to day life prior to java 8. The drawbacks of the Data class is 
-> mutable
-> non thread safe
-> bad design
-> confusig

LocalDate class provides you clean, immutable and thread safe dates instances by which you can work with dates comfortable.
if you want only dates, then go with LocalDate=LocalDate.now();
if you want only time, then go with LocalTime lt=LocalTime.now();
if you want both date and time, then go with LocalDateTime ldt=LocalDateTime.now();
if you want both the time stamps then you can go with Instant instant=Intant.now() which wil give you time stamps.
